WEBVTT

00:03:59.556 --> 00:04:03.156
Cunning folk, cunning women
were wise women.

00:04:03.196 --> 00:04:05.756
And in Scotland still today,
if you can something,

00:04:05.796 --> 00:04:07.636
it means you know something.

00:04:07.676 --> 00:04:09.036
“I ken this.”

00:04:09.076 --> 00:04:11.716
It also gave us "queen" and "cow,"

00:04:11.756 --> 00:04:15.916
slightly bizarre, which is slightly
less highbrow, but --

00:04:18.396 --> 00:04:22.396
It turns up again in the
Middle Ages in "quaint,"

00:04:22.436 --> 00:04:24.596
which means "knowledge"
and also means "cunt."

00:04:24.636 --> 00:04:26.596
It has a Latin variation as well,

00:04:26.596 --> 00:04:28.956
"cunnis," which also means "cunt,"

00:04:28.996 --> 00:04:31.076
which turns up all over the Roman world,